// The us layout under xkeyboard-config 2.48 evdev rules, pc105 model, compiled by
// xkbcli compile-keymap. xkeyboard-config is distributed under its MIT/X11-style
// licence; see https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xkeyboard-config/xkeyboard-config.
// Regenerate with: xkbcli compile-keymap --rules evdev --model pc105 --layout us
// Then trim it to what tests/evdev_codes.rs reads: keep the keycodes the test names,
// keep the symbols of every key whose first group carries a keysym the test checks,
// and leave xkb_types and xkb_compatibility empty.
